{
  "dom_id": "step-144951",
  "name": "Example: \n                    Identifying Necessary or Sufficient Conditions From Implications",
  "problem": "$\\qquad$ $(A=\\overline{B}) \\Rightarrow (A\\cap B = \\emptyset)$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the true implication above?\n\nI. $A=\\overline{B}$ is a **necessary** condition for $A\\cap B = \\emptyset$\n\nII. $A=\\overline{B}$ is a **sufficient** condition for $A\\cap B = \\emptyset$\n\nIII. $A\\cap B = \\emptyset$ is a **necessary** condition for $A=\\overline{B}$\n\nIV. $A\\cap B = \\emptyset$ is a **sufficient** condition for $A=\\overline{B}$",
  "worked_solution": "Given that the implication $S \\Rightarrow N$ is true, we have the following:\n\n- $S$ being true *guarantees* that $N$ must also be true. Therefore, $S$ is a *sufficient condition* for $N.$\n\n- For $S$ to be true, it is *necessary* that $N$ is true. Therefore, $N$ is a *necessary condition* for $S.$ However, note that $N$ being true does *not* guarantee that $S$ is true.\n\nThese ideas can be summarized as follows:\n\n$$\n\\textbf{S}\\textrm{ufficient} \\: \\Rightarrow \\: \\textbf{N}\\textrm{ecessary}.\n$$\n\n  \n\nIn our case,\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{\\big( \\, A=\\overline{B} \\, \\big)}_{\\large\\textrm{sufficient}} \n\\: \\Rightarrow \\: \n\\underbrace{\\big( \\, A\\cap B = \\emptyset \\, \\big)}_{\\large\\textrm{necessary}}\n$$\n\nis a true statement. Therefore:\n\n- Statement II is true. $A=\\overline{B}$ is a **sufficient** condition for $A\\cap B = \\emptyset.$\n\n- Statement III is true. $A\\cap B = \\emptyset$ is a **necessary** condition for $A=\\overline{B}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
  "html": "<div id=\"step-144951\" class=\"step\" style=\"display: block\" stepid=\"144951\" steptype=\"example\" contentid=\"12758\">\n            <div class=\"stepHeader\">\n                <div class=\"stepName\">\n                    Example: \n                    <a id=\"stepAnchor-144951\" class=\"stepAnchor\" style=\"font-weight: normal;\" name=\"step-2\">Identifying Necessary or Sufficient Conditions From Implications</a> \n                </div>      \n                <div class=\"helpButton\" stepid=\"144951\">?</div>\n            </div>\n            \n            <div class=\"exampleQuestion\">\n                <style type=\"text/css\">\n                            .mjpage .MJX-monospace {\n                            font-family: monospace\n                            }\n\n                            .mjpage .MJX-sans-serif {\n                            font-family: sans-serif\n                            }\n\n                            .mjpage {\n                            display: inline;\n                            font-style: normal;\n                            font-weight: normal;\n                            line-height: normal;\n                            font-size: 100%;\n                            font-size-adjust: none;\n                            text-indent: 0;\n                            text-align: left;\n                            text-transform: none;\n                            letter-spacing: normal;\n                            word-spacing: normal;\n                            word-wrap: normal;\n                            white-space: nowrap;\n                            float: none;\n                            direction: ltr;\n                            max-width: none;\n                            max-height: none;\n                            min-width: 0;\n                            min-height: 0;\n                            border: 0;\n                            padding: 0;\n                            margin: 0